# Blinded raw observation packages

Document ID: `reiyah.perception-observation.interface`

Version: `0.1.0`

Lifecycle status: `exploratory`

This offline Engine component constructs the material for unassisted object discovery in the
[selected perception study](../../../docs/PERCEPTION_DECISION_ARCHITECTURE_2026-09-09.md).
It projects an existing raw-window population into neutral capture identifiers, permitted raw
evidence and relative spatial/time operands. The private source mapping stays outside the
reviewer directory. No reviewer observations are generated by packaging.

## Interface

The request is closed: only these fields are permitted. Ellipses stand for exact private file
paths and SHA-256 values, not usable defaults. `package_id` is 32 lowercase hexadecimal
characters identifying this delivery; it is not a study-selection seed.

```json
{
  "artifact_id": "reiyah.perception-observation.request",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "package_id": "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
  "window_report": {"path": "...", "byte_size": 123, "sha256": "..."},
  "geometry_report": {"path": "...", "byte_size": 123, "sha256": "..."},
  "inventory": {"path": "...", "byte_size": 123, "sha256": "..."},
  "raw_root": "/private/raw"
}
```

Use the versions in [requirements.txt](requirements.txt), installed in the caller's environment.
All input artifact JSON rejects duplicate properties, floating-point tokens and nonfinite
values. Every source descriptor includes the exact byte size and digest; the source is
snapshotted and verified before parsing. Source payload bytes are reopened and reverified
against the inventory immediately before disclosure and decoding.

```sh
python -B -m tools.perception_observation build \
  --request /private/request.json --request-sha256 ACTUAL_REQUEST_SHA256 \
  --output /private/new-reviewer-package --custody /private/new-custody.json

python -B -m tools.perception_observation verify \
  --package /private/new-reviewer-package --seal-sha256 SEPARATELY_RETAINED_SEAL_SHA256
```

Output parents must exist. The package directory and custody file must both be new; custody
must lie outside the package tree. The verifier requires the expected seal digest from
separate custody. Reading the package's own digest back to itself is not a provenance check.
Exit 0 means the requested build or verification completed. It does not mean all evidence is
available or any human review has occurred. Exit 2 reports an invalid request, source, binding,
disclosure or file operation. A failed build may leave a partial directory; it cannot be reused
and has no usable completion seal.

## Information boundary

The reviewer directory contains exactly `manifest.json`, `READ_ME.txt`, `SEAL.json` and an
`assets` directory. Its manifest has a closed, typed structure enforced by
[contract.py](../../../tools/perception_observation/contract.py).

| Disclosed | Separate private custody only |
| --- | --- |
| Sequential neutral window/capture IDs | Source scene, sample, calibration and pose identifiers |
| Seven sensor orientations and nominal image dimensions | Source filenames, absolute paths and operational catalogs |
| Relative microsecond capture times in the closed ±2-second window | Absolute clocks and global poses |
| Nominal sensor-to-anchor-ego matrices and camera intrinsics, or explicit unavailable states | Original upstream geometry, identities, private diagnostics and source mappings |
| Raw camera evidence and unchanged lidar point fields in a fixed wrapper | Annotations, detector names/scores/boxes, historical candidate rankings and keyframe flags |
| Recording-stream boundary state and fixed uncertainty explanation | Free-form upstream prose, including fields added by another tool |

The producer constructs the permitted projection field by field. It does not delete a few
known detector fields from a larger source object and then share the remainder. Tests change
forbidden metadata, source filenames and absolute clock origins while holding permitted
observations fixed: the complete reviewer file tree must remain byte-identical.

This boundary restricts method and reference hints. It does not anonymize public source data:
raw imagery, nominal sensor geometry and file hashes can reveal its identity. Nor does it prove
the absence of information encoded in pixels or point values. Reviewers still require the
study's procedural blinding and staged information controls.

## Population, geometry and formats

The geometry report must bind the exact requested window report, and the window report must
bind the requested inventory. Window identities, intervals, occurrence order and complete
capture union must agree. Required channel, time, calibration and pose joins must agree.
Duplicate captures within a window and inconsistent cross-window aliases are invalid.
An empty channel remains represented; an absent capture does not become an empty sensor output.
No new scene or anchor is selected here.

The upstream [geometry computation](../../perception-geometry/0.1.0/README.md) remains a bound
dependency. This consumer checks its joins, state types and matrix forms; it does not repeat
the source-metadata replay or independently re-prove the transform computation. Available
matrices contain reduced rational strings, at most 256 digits each, with magnitude at most
10^12. Rigid transforms must preserve orthonormality and handedness exactly. Intrinsics retain
the positive-focal, upper-triangular pinhole form.

Matrices map homogeneous column coordinates at capture time from the sensor frame to the
anchor ego frame. They do not move objects forward or backward in time. Physical calibration,
clock accuracy, exposure duration, per-point times, online availability, object motion and
physical reference completeness remain unmeasured or unestablished.

Camera bytes are preserved exactly when they pass full RGB decoding and the restricted
`unassisted_raw_relative_time.0.1.0` disclosure profile. The full JPEG marker stream is checked,
including the end of the entropy-coded scan. The profile permits one initial basic JFIF APP0
header without a thumbnail and one baseline interleaved scan. It refuses other application
headers, comments, progressive scans, post-scan payloads and concatenated/trailing bytes.
A file outside that profile is withheld; it is never stripped or recompressed to fit.
This intentionally narrower policy is not a general JPEG conformance test.

Lidar files use PLY `binary_little_endian 1.0`, with one vertex element and five float
properties: x, y, z, intensity and ring. The fixed header precedes the unchanged source
little-endian float32 records. Coordinates remain in the original sensor frame. There is no
filtering, downsampling, sorting, accumulation, surface reconstruction or invented acquisition
time. Every source point field must be finite and the nonempty body must contain complete
20-byte records. The [source basis](source-basis.json) records private custody of the primary
format references and the existing nuScenes convention dependency.

## Distinct evidence states

| State | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `delivered` | Current bytes match the inventory and pass the applicable disclosure and decoding profile; an exact asset descriptor is present |
| `not_listed` | The required capture has no asset identity in the supplied inventory |
| `unavailable` | The inventory explicitly declares no retained payload |
| `missing` | A retained path is currently absent |
| `invalid` | A raw path/type, byte count, digest or I/O check fails |
| `sensor_invalid` | Verified bytes fail the applicable sensor decoding/record check |
| `not_checked` | The required decoder or its supported runtime configuration is unavailable |
| `withheld` | Camera bytes are outside the restricted metadata disclosure profile, including an incomplete profile parse; no claim of general JPEG invalidity is implied |

Only `delivered` includes an asset. Every other state retains the capture's place and relative
time without a substitute value. Missing and invalid calibration/intrinsic operands retain
their own state, separately from raw availability. A structurally verified package containing
unavailable evidence does not certify review adequacy.

## Completion and checks

The producer creates a new private directory, writes its assets, closed manifest and fixed
guide, and retains separate custody. It writes `SEAL.json` last using a non-overwriting atomic
file operation. This is an explicit completion boundary, not an atomic transaction across two
locations. A seal binds the manifest and guide; the manifest binds every delivered asset.

The verifier checks the separately expected seal hash, the closed manifest, exact directory
membership, every file's digest and size, and the raw format/decoder checks. Symlink paths,
extra annotation or custody files, omitted assets and changed bytes are rejected. It verifies
the bytes it opens; it does not guarantee the directory cannot change after verification.

Requests are at most 4 MiB; window/geometry reports and the output manifest are each at most
128 MiB, inventories 64 MiB, raw files 64 MiB, and total declared evidence 2 GiB. Packages
are bounded to 128 windows, 10,000 distinct captures and 50,000 capture occurrences. Larger
jobs are rejected, not truncated. Images are bounded to 8192 per side and 32 million pixels.
The producer retains code and runtime identities before/after processing in private custody.
This is an offline application, not an operating-system isolation or malicious-host guarantee.

The [tests](../../../tests/test_perception_observation.py) cover noninterference, full
population joins, same-byte decoding, matrix/type defects, missingness, metadata after scans,
format roundtrips, resource limits, separate custody, interruption, output reuse and tampering.
Independent human reviewers, locked discovery records, a competent comparator, adjudication
and the complete study freeze remain separate requirements.
